nodecode-nvidia-broadcast is a rewrite of NousResearch's NousResearch/hermes-nvidia:

  https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-nvidia
  commit de75692b479dc88b95e428a9cb25091d3fb0e327
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Nous Research (the licence the plugin declares in its plugin.json; the repository carried no LICENSE file)

Rewritten: the MCP gateway's ten tools - get_broadcast_state, set_effects,
describe_effects, list_devices, set_active_device, set_camera_resolution,
submit_file_processing, get_file_processing_jobs, wait_for_processing_update and
control_file_processing_jobs - with their argument names, argument shapes and
answer shapes, including the _version 1 every file tool carries, the effect
params nested under "params", the device ids that must be re-read before every
switch, the frame rate that is never guessed, and the batchId that groups one
submit's siblings. Also rewritten: the connection the skill described, as a
streamable-HTTP MCP client in Common Lisp - one POST per JSON-RPC message, the
Mcp-Session-Id the initialize answer issues echoed on every later one, the
answers read from either an application/json body or a server-sent event - and
the guidance the skill gave the model about reading the gateway's answers
(requiresUserInput, failed[], skipped[], mixed, the retryable -32603), which is
this cell's (help :nvidia-broadcast) manual. The Python-free original carried no
code to port: it was one MCP declaration, one skill and its references, and the
cell holds the same endpoint and the same tools.

Left out: everything the skill did around the app rather than through the
gateway. It read the installed build's ProductVersion, launched the app with
--launch-hidden when it was not running, discovered a port other than 18100 from
the base64 port record the app writes, carried the WSL networking guidance, and,
with an explicit yes from the user, downloaded NVIDIA's own installer from
NVIDIA's update service, verified its length, SHA-512 and Authenticode signer,
and launched it. Those are the operator's side of the original - it changed the
machine, not the effects - and a cell leaves them to the person: the app has to
be installed at 2.3 or newer and running, and the port record reduces to the
url setting.
